cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this pipeline, please cite it as below and cite the associated article."
title: "glaucoma-AFO: an R pipeline for multi-omics analysis of trabecular meshwork mechanotransduction and extracellular matrix remodelling in primary open-angle glaucoma"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Xu
    given-names: Weihai
    affiliation: "Department of Ophthalmology, Binhai County People's Hospital, Kangda College of Nanjing Medical University, Yancheng 224500, Jiangsu Province, China"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-10
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A numbered R pipeline (steps 00-17) covering bulk transcriptome preprocessing
  and differential expression, WGCNA, pathway activity and deconvolution,
  machine-learning signature construction with Harrell optimism correction,
  single-cell and cell-cell communication analysis, cross-species concordance,
  colocalisation, TWAS, two-sample and mediation Mendelian randomisation,
  in silico perturbation with label-permutation and multiverse robustness checks,
  and a results ledger that maps every reported number back to the output file
  and field from which it was derived.
keywords:
  - primary open-angle glaucoma
  - trabecular meshwork
  - extracellular matrix
  - mechanotransduction
  - Mendelian randomization
  - single-cell transcriptomics
  - reproducibility
